// Stage controller F1b (area clear 47da4..47eac with 4b6e4/4b6ec, 1c5b0, 1bee4, ca48 and 9056) through
// run_animation_machine only. A frame is one run from a callback PC to the dispatcher return 2ac2 (480bc -> 480f0 RTS);
// the next frame is the declared direct re-entry A6=100b30, A5=108000, A7=10effc, LONG 10effc=2ac2, PC=LONG (A6) with the
// other registers and C kept; the last frame stops at 477ee (F1c, no executor). Child completion 62(A6) and 10dd44 (and
// 10d68e in typed fixtures) change only through declared host writes between frames. All inputs are declared fixtures:
// zero RAM plus the PUTS rows, declared registers and the return LONG at A7 (stack inside work RAM at 10effc). The 480bc
// frames use the F1a frame base (player nodes, U7 buffer rows, U2/U3 records) and the 28ae allocator rows. Synthetic
// typed physical bytes (not a ROM oracle): the U6 default mask row 49ab0 (contract bytes 10 20 40 80).
// The FIXTURES/PHASES/CHAINS/DIGESTS/BLOCKS tables were produced from the original code bytes (Unicorn M68000 on the
// canonical BE ROM, stack in work RAM, SR read only to seed and check C) and every phase and every chain frame was
// cross-checked against this machine with the full physical ROM before being recorded (16 registers, PC, status, bank,
// ordered ports, external reads, the whole 64 KiB RAM, and a known machine C against the original C). Error rows are
// checked errors of this machine (the original takes an address error, TRAP #15 or runs into code without an executor).
// Long change lists and port lists are recorded as FNV-1a hashes; a chain frame is recorded as the FNV-1a digest of
// (RAM, D0-D7/A0-A7, PC, bank, reads as BE LONGs, status, carry, ordered (size, address, value) port bytes).
